* Wed Oct 07 2026 Joachim Klahr <klahr@r8.rs> 0.5.0-1
- mosh, which keeps the session through network changes, sleep and dead
  spots and through a restart of the app, with typing shown before the
  server echoes it on slow links
- Files on the server: browse, download, open, upload, rename and delete
  files and folders, also straight from the session menu, and upload
  files shared from other apps
- Coding agents such as Claude Code and Codex show what they are doing in
  the session and notify on questions and finished turns, with buttons to
  allow or refuse permission requests, through a plugin for the server
- Programs can send notifications with OSC 9 or OSC 777
- Snippets of commands typed with one tap, per host or for all, and the
  history of what was typed in the session
- Hardware keyboard shortcuts: Alt and Meta, Ctrl with symbols,
  Ctrl+Shift+C/V, Ctrl+Tab and Ctrl+PgUp/PgDn between connections and
  Ctrl+Shift+T for a new one
- Key toolbar above the keyboard or at the top, Ctrl and Alt lock when
  tapped twice, drag the arrows key to move the cursor
- Any monospace font on the device, with Nerd Fonts symbols, and color
  schemes imported from iTerm2, Alacritty, Windows Terminal, Xresources
  or base16
- Save or share the scrollback, log sessions to Documents/Longterm, and
  select text from the screen in a window of its own
- Certificate login, remote port forwards, a SOCKS proxy, environment
  variables, keepalive and connect timeouts, Wake-on-LAN and attaching to
  a tmux session, per host or per connection
- Hosts in groups and favorites, most recent first, with search
- Install keys on a host from the app, like ssh-copy-id
- Back up everything into one file encrypted with a passphrase, and
  restore from it
- Lock the app with a code, and show host key fingerprints as QR codes
- Key passphrases are asked for before connecting, so a slow answer no
  longer times out the login, and are not asked again on reconnects
- Typing exit goes back to the connections
- Fix swiping when all connections are disconnected

* Fri Oct 02 2026 Joachim Klahr <klahr@r8.rs> 0.4.0-1
- Fix shell output lost or replaced by old lines when the keyboard opens
  or closes, also while a full-screen program like vim or htop is shown
- Typing goes to the connection on screen after swiping to it, without
  tapping the terminal first
- Swipe the keyboard down to hide it, tap the terminal or the toolbar to
  bring it back
- Scrolling no longer jumps while output arrives, keeps going after a
  flick and is not taken over by the swipe between connections
- Scrolling in full-screen programs moves the program instead of showing
  older output, with the mouse wheel when the program asks for it
- Disconnected connections are left out of the swipe between connections,
  connected ones show their status in green
- Login prompts use the server's own labels, and a server that only
  accepts keys says so
- Fix operating system icons

* Tue Sep 29 2026 Joachim Klahr <klahr@r8.rs> 0.3.0-1
- Show the operating system of hosts and connections as an icon
- About page with the licenses of the app and the components it uses
- Fix memory corruption on some escape sequences from the server
- Fix a crash on keys encrypted with AES-GCM or ChaCha20-Poly1305, which
  are now refused with a hint to re-encrypt them; security keys (FIDO)
  are refused as well
- Show server prompts and messages, host and key names as plain text
- Pasted text can no longer end bracketed paste early
- Fix connections leaking on disconnect, stalls from port forwards and
  agent forwarding, and reconnects after disconnecting on purpose
- Notice frozen connections within a minute and a half, and try the next
  address sooner when one does not answer
- Faster ssh_config import that reads quotes and comments like OpenSSH,
  exported configs can no longer carry extra lines from pasted values
- Deleting a host closes its connections
- Fix trusting changed host keys, removing known hosts, ports outside
  1-65535 and duplicate connection names
- Import keys with a passphrase without freezing the app

* Tue Sep 29 2026 Joachim Klahr <klahr@r8.rs> 0.2.1-1
- Fix crashes and hangs on some output from the server and on resizes,
  found by fuzzing the terminal emulator
- Keep the app responsive and its memory use low when a server floods output
- Disconnect right away from servers that stop answering
- Encrypted keys can be imported without their passphrase, it is then asked
  for on every connect
- Connections follow changes to their saved host, deleted keys are removed
  from the hosts using them
- Ask for missing or wrong passwords in the session, optionally remembering
  them
- Scrolled-back terminals stay put while output arrives, with a button back
  to the latest output
- Title bar and thumbnails in the session's color scheme, faster session
  switching

* Mon Sep 28 2026 Joachim Klahr <klahr@r8.rs> 0.2.0-1
- Keyboard-interactive login, and password prompts in the session with
  an option to remember the password
- Jump hosts, local port forwards and agent forwarding per host
- Reconnect automatically when the network drops or changes
- Ed25519, ECDSA and RSA key generation, and private key export
- Known hosts list, and hosts import and export as ssh_config
- Search in the scrollback, open links, clipboard from the server (OSC 52)
- Configurable key toolbar with Alt, Home/End, PgUp/PgDn and F1-F12
- Terminal bell vibrates, or notifies when the session is not on screen
- Per-session color schemes, and Gruvbox Dark, Nord, Solarized Dark and
  Solarized Light
- Live session thumbnails in the connection list

* Fri Sep 25 2026 Joachim Klahr <klahr@r8.rs> 0.1.1-1
- Fix app not starting from the launcher

* Thu Sep 24 2026 Joachim Klahr <klahr@r8.rs> 0.1.0-1
- First release
- Multiple SSH connections with switching and a cover overview
- xterm-256color terminal with scrollback, pinch to zoom, copy and paste
- Saved hosts, Ed25519 key generation and import, remembered passwords
  kept in the Sailfish Secrets keychain
- Color schemes: Default, Catppuccin Mocha and Dracula
